          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Cartan connection
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            equipped with a certain compatibility condition with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of the manifold. It combines the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            with that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soldering+form"} soldering form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – such as notably (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"}> pseudo
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"}> Riemannian geometry
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+geometry"} conformal geometry
            and many more (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#TableOfExamples"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            data, i.e. in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            = succeed "-data." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+formulation+of+gravity"} first order formulation of gravity
            in terms of Cartan connections has been one of the historical motivations (
            %a{:href => "#Cartan23"}> Cartan 23
            ).
          %p
            In a little bit more detail, a Cartan connection on a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \hookrightarrow G
            is data that identifies all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+spaces"} tangent spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_x X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with the tangent space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h} = T_{e H} (G/H)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
          %p
            Therefore a manifold equipped with a Cartan connection is also called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            (see also there), a generalization (globalization) of the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
          %p
            In yet a little bit more detail, an
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \hookrightarrow G)
              \-Cartan connection
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+structure+groups"} reduction of its structure group
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to G
            and such that the connection 1-form linearly identifies each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_x X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with the tangent space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h} = T_{e H} (G/H)
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The concept essentially originates around (
            %a{:href => "#Cartan23"}> Cartan 23
            ), but the formulation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            and in fact the terminology “Cartan connection” is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"} Charles Ehresmann
            who formulated principal connections as what, in turn, today are called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connections"} Ehresmann connections
            (
            %a{:href => "#Ehresmann50"}> Ehresmann 50
            ).
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Ehresmann50"}> Ehresmann 50
            ) Cartan’s ideas are formalized (see
            %a{:href => "#Marle14"} Marle 14, page 9, 10
            for review) by saying that an
            = succeed "-Cartan" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G \hookrightarrow H)
            = succeed "-Ehresmann" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            equipped with an
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#traditional Traditional
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \hookrightarrow G
            a sub-Lie group. (So that we may think of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            as a
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h} \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{g}
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
          %p
            There are various equivalent forms of the definition of Cartan connections. The following one characterizes it as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            equipped with extra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure+and+property"} structure and property
          #Traditional.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-Cartan" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \hookrightarrow G)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is;
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∇
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                  on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p such that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      there is a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+structure+groups"} reduction of structure groups
                      along
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi H
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi G
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \hookrightarrow G
                  %li
                    %p
                      for each point
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                      the canonical composite (for any local trivialization)
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi x
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ∇
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo →
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi 𝔥
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            T_x X \stackrel{\nabla}{\to} \mathfrak{g} \to \mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h}
                    %p
                      is an
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p More explicitly for various component-realizations of principal connections, this means the following:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  In terms of
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"}> Ehresmann connection
                    \-data
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Traditional"}
                  says that an
                  = succeed "-Cartan" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H\hookrightarrow G)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  on a
                  = succeed "-principal" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                  together with an
                  = succeed "-principal" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                  and an
                  = succeed "-equivariant" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Q
                        %mo →
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Q\to P
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast A
                  yields an isomorphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi Q
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Q
                          %mo ×
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Q \simeq Q\times \mathfrak{g}
                %p
                  In this form the definition is due to (
                  %a{:href => "#Ehresmann50"}> Ehresmann 50
                  ), recalled in (
                  %a{:href => "#Marle14"}> Marle 14, def. 4
                  ). Often this definition is stated by describing
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast A
                  directly without mentioning of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Sharpe"} Sharpe 97, section 5.3, def. 3.1
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "#CapSlovak09"} Cap-Slovák 09, 1.5.1
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
                  but
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast A
                  is not.
              %li
                %p
                  In terms of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                      data
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Traditional"}
                  says that an
                  = succeed "-Cartan" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H\hookrightarrow G)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                  equipped with 1-forms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
